---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Software">
    <h1 class="text-gradient">Software By Us</h1>
    
    <div style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        <img src="/images/Asterix26_Dogmatix.webp" style="width: 200px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;" />
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-gradient">Asterics Software Suite (.NET, Windows)</h2>
    <p style="text-align: justify; margin-bottom: 3rem;">
        We have a collection of <i>in-house</i> software powering our analysis, named 
        after the comic series Asterix the Gaul.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-gradient">PyGaulics (Python, Cross-platform)</h2>
    <p style="text-align: justify">
        PyGaulics was developed as a supplement for the Asterics suite, an auxiliary for the software named after the Gauls, 
        and evolved into a stand-alone image analytics/spatial analysis powered by PyTorch, PyTorch Geometric and other 
        scientific imaging packages.
    </p>
</Layout>
